# Word's lock file, present whenever the walkthrough is open for reading.
# Untracked but not ignored, it rode along with any `git add -A` — and a
# committed ~$ file tells everyone who clones that the document is locked by
# someone who left.
~$*

# Copy written for the hackathon submission form, kept beside the document it
# summarises for convenience. Not committed: it would be a third overlapping
# description of the project after the README and the walkthrough, and the one
# most likely to go stale first.
docs/project-description.md
